          "speaker": "Sophie",
          "text": "No, it was yesterday."
        },
        {
          "id": "p1-31",
          "speaker": "Man",
          "text": "Right. And do you usually buy your tickets at the station?"
        },
        {
          "id": "p1-32",
          "speaker": "Sophie",
          "text": "Well, I do usually but the ticket office closes early and I hate using ticket machines. I think ticket offices should be open for longer hours. There’s always a queue for the machines and they’re often out of order."
        },
        {
          "id": "p1-33",
          "speaker": "Man",
          "text": "A lot of customers are saying the same thing."
        },
        {
          "id": "p1-34",
          "speaker": "Sophie",
          "text": "So to answer your question … I got an e-ticket online."
        },
        {
          "id": "p1-35",
          "speaker": "Man",
          "text": "OK. Thank you. Now I’d like to ask you about your satisfaction with your journey. So what would you say you were most satisfied with today?"
        },
        {
          "id": "p1-36",
          "speaker": "Sophie",
          "text": "Well, I like the wifi on the train. It’s improved a lot. It makes it easier for me to work if I want to."
        },
        {
          "id": "p1-37",
          "speaker": "Man",
          "text": "That’s the first time today anyone’s mentioned that. It’s good to get some positive feedback on that."
        },
        {
          "id": "p1-38",
          "speaker": "Sophie",
          "text": "Mmm."
        },
        {
          "id": "p1-39",
          "speaker": "Man",
          "text": "And, is there anything you weren’t satisfied with?"
        },
        {
          "id": "p1-40",
          "speaker": "Sophie",
          "text": "Well, normally, the trains run on time and are pretty reliable but today there was a delay; the train was about 15 minutes behind schedule."
        },
        {
          "id": "p1-41",
          "speaker": "Man",
          "text": "OK. I’ll put that down. Now I’d also like to ask about the facilities at this station. You’ve probably noticed that the whole station’s been upgraded. What are you most satisfied with?"
        },
        {
          "id": "p1-42",
          "speaker": "Sophie",
          "text": "I think the best thing is that they’ve improved the amount of information about train times etc. that’s given to passengers - it’s much clearer - before there was only one board and I couldn’t always see it properly - which was frustrating."
        },
        {
          "id": "p1-43",
          "speaker": "Man",
          "text": "That’s good. And is there anything you’re not satisfied with?"
        },
        {
          "id": "p1-44",
          "speaker": "Sophie",
          "text": "Let’s see … I think things have generally improved a lot. The trains are much more modern and I like the new café. But one thing is that there aren’t enough places to sit down, especially on the platforms."
        },
        {
          "id": "p1-45",
          "speaker": "Man",
          "text": "OK - so I’ll put ‘seating’ down, shall I, as the thing you’re least satisfied with?"
        },
        {
          "id": "p1-46",
          "speaker": "Sophie",
          "text": "Yes, OK."
        },
        {
          "id": "p1-47",
          "speaker": "Man",
          "text": "Can I ask your opinion about some of the other facilities? We’d like feedback on whether people are satisfied, dissatisfied or neither satisfied nor dissatisfied."
        },
        {
          "id": "p1-48",
          "speaker": "Sophie",
          "text": "OK."
        },
        {
          "id": "p1-49",
          "speaker": "Man",
          "text": "What about the parking at the station?"
        },
        {
          "id": "p1-50",
          "speaker": "Sophie",
          "text": "Well to be honest, I don’t really have an opinion as I never use it."
        },
        {
          "id": "p1-51",
          "speaker": "Man",
          "text": "So, neither satisfied nor dissatisfied for that then."
        },
